{#- MCP servers, keyless or credentialed. One template, one param file per
    server, switched by `authentication`:

      none    — public upstream, nothing injected. A customer enrols and the
                tools work.
      apikey  — the customer brings a token. The channel carries
                `${ customer_secrets.<secret_name> }` and the gateway resolves
                it per caller (unitysvc/unitysvc#1819).

    Two params make a service testable without a real third-party account,
    both borrowed from the notify services:

      base_url_secret_name — makes the *endpoint* a customer secret defaulting
                             to the official upstream. Set that secret to
                             https://mcp.unitysvc.dev/mcp/private and calls go
                             to the mock instead of the real provider.
      secret_default       — appends `?? default` to the credential, so the
                             reference resolves with nothing provisioned.

    Together they mean the real GitHub/Linear/... services can be exercised end
    to end — same spec, same channel, same injection path — with the upstream
    swapped underneath. Neither changes anything for a customer who sets
    neither secret: they get the official endpoint and their own token.

    That one reference is also what *classifies* the channel: derive_channel_type
    scans the config for the substring `customer_secrets.` and, with a static
    base_url, calls it byok. The type is derived, never declared, so there is no
    second place to keep in sync (unitysvc/unitysvc#1305).

    Enrollment is required either way. A credential alone gets the customer
    nothing — build_mcp_context joins on an active enrollment, so the tools
    appear only once both exist. That "secrets + enroll" state is what
    unitysvc/unitysvc#1813 is designed around.

    There is deliberately no tool manifest here: the gateway serves tools/list
    live from the upstream (unitysvc/unitysvc#1833 — a pinned copy is a
    permanent cache that drifts silently, and for `apikey` servers the toolset
    varies with the credential's scopes anyway). -#}
{%- set authentication = authentication | default('none') %}
{
  "capabilities": [
    "mcp"
  ],
  "description": {{ description | tojson }},
{%- if logo is defined and logo %}
  {#- Convenience field: ingest turns it into a logo document, and the uploader
      mirrors the external URL onto platform S3. -#}
  "logo": {{ logo | tojson }},
{%- endif %}
  "name": "{{ name.split('/')[-1] }}",
  "payout_price": {
    "description": "No seller payout",
    "percentage": "0.00",
    "type": "revenue_share"
  },
  "service_type": "mcp",
  "status": "ready",
  "summary": {{ summary | tojson }},
  "tags": {{ (tags | default(['mcp'])) | tojson }},
  "time_created": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z",
  "upstream_access_config": {
    "{{ namespace }}": {
      "access_method": "mcp",
{%- if authentication == 'apikey' %}
      {#- The customer's own token. Resolved per call against the calling
          customer's secrets — the catalog only ever stores this reference,
          and the rendered value never reaches the context response. -#}
      "api_key": "${ customer_secrets.{{ secret_name }}{% if secret_default is defined and secret_default %} ?? {{ secret_default }}{% endif %} }",
      "auth_mode": "customer_token",
{%- else %}
      "auth_mode": "none",
{%- endif %}
      {#- The endpoint is itself overridable, defaulting to the official
          upstream — the notify idiom (unitysvc-services-notify). Point
          `base_url_secret_name` at the mock and the service is testable end to
          end without a real third-party account; leave it unset and every
          caller gets the real provider. -#}
{%- if base_url_secret_name is defined and base_url_secret_name %}
      "base_url": "${ customer_secrets.{{ base_url_secret_name }} ?? {{ upstream_url }} }",
{%- else %}
      "base_url": "{{ upstream_url }}",
{%- endif %}
      "timeout_ms": {{ timeout_ms | default(30000) }},
      "transport": "streamable_http"
    }
  }
}
